        <body>
            <div xml:id="d46">

                <pb facs="0166" n="72" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg72"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Denby, chargé, to
                        Mr. Olney.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-05-30"><hi rendition="#italic">May 30, 1896</hi></date>.
                        (Received July 11.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2536.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my dispatch, No. 2533 of the
                    23d instant, regarding the Kiangyin riots, in which the property of the Southern
                    Presbyterian Mission was destroyed, I have the honor to inclose herewith a copy
                    of a dispatch received to-day from Consul Jones at Chinkiang, giving a full
                    account of the incident, and of the steps he has taken to secure protection and
                    redress. It is believed that there will be no difficulty in reaching a
                    satisfactory local settlement of this case.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Denby</hi>, Jr.,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chargé d’Affaires ad interim.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d46-a1.xml" xpointer="d46-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
